  <running_head>EPIGRAM. A. FAYI.</running_head>
  <bottom_margin>
    <signature>T</signature>
  </bottom_margin>
  <main_text>
    <l>Fontes ducit originis.</l>
    <l>Dic te cœlitus editam:</l>
    <l>Dic te spiritibus parem</l>
    <l>Addendamque piis: Deum</l>
    <l>Natam nosse: perennibus</l>
    <l>Donandam superum boni:</l>
    <l>Te cœli superas domos,</l>
    <l>Latos aëris &amp; lares,</l>
    <l>Altos Oceani sinus,</l>
    <l>Terræ multifidas plagas,</l>
    <l>Lustrantem citius Noti</l>
    <l>Alis diffugientibus:</l>
    <l>Immotiqué typum Dei</l>
    <l>Gestantem: indocilem pati</l>
    <l>Fessi incommoda corporis,</l>
    <l>Moti robore non suo:</l>
    <l>Te rasæ tabulæ æmulam:</l>
    <l>Nullis illita quæ notis,</l>
    <l>Nullas non recipit notas.</l>
    <l>Nec vero memorem tace</l>
    <l>Thesaurum tibi ditatum,</l>
    <l>In quem, quæ cupis ingeris:</l>
    <l>Ex quo, quæ cupis eruis.</l>
    <l>Hinc præsentia iungere</l>
    <l>Ventris potes, &amp; dies</l>
    <l>Lapsos nectere fas tibi:</l>
    <l>Vt, seu verba loqui libet,</l>
    <l>Seu quid consilio aggredi,</l>
    <l>Libres pondera singula,</l>
    <l>Res prudens &amp; agas tuas:</l>
    <l>Hæc tecum reputans simul</l>
    <l>Eia mens mea tollere</l>
    <l>Orbes in superos leuis</l>
  </main_text>
  <notes>Lines are verse; the printed text is partly faint and blurred at the left edge and in the lower lines, with some letters doubtful (e.g. "Natam", "ditatum", "Libres", "leuis"). The line "Orbes in superos leuis" has a damaged initial letter. The mark "T" at the foot is a signature.</notes>
</page>
